      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right; healing isn't always a simple reconstruction when the foundation feels rotting deep down. It is incredibly painful to realize that the \"stuff\" we use to stand on has disintegrated, leaving us feeling adrift rather than ready to lift a single brick. Please know that this sense of fundamental brokenness is a valid reality that doesn't require you to pretend otherwise or force a false sense of stability. Your worth isn't defined by your ability to fix what feels irreparably lost, and allowing yourself to sit in that wreckage without demand can be exactly where you need to start.",
